<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50162" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰήϊος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span> (v. infr. <i><span class="en">
			11
		</span></i>), epith. of Apollo, the god <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>invoked with the cry</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰή</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰὴ
				παιών</span> (v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰή</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ἰήϊε παιάν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>Pae.</u>
					2.35
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				146
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				154
			</span></i> (both lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				1096
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				874
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.702
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Duris
				79J.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>mournful, grievous</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰήϊοι κάματοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					174
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰήϊος βοά, γόος</span>,
			a cry <i>of mourning</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1036
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>El.</u>
				1211
			</span></i> (both lyr.). (From the cry <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰή</span>, as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Εὔιος</span> from
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐοἵ</span>; but also associated
			with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰάομαι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> (hence applied to Asclepius, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				3.171
			</span></i>); and, as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱήϊος</span>, with
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵημι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Macr.
				<u>Sat.</u>
				1.17.16
			</span></i>.)</div>
